\ Ms. Pac-Man: the mazes, the rules, the synthesizer patches and music, and the
\ 2D drawing, shared by examples/ms-pac-man.telic (2D) and
\ examples/ms-pac-man-3d.telic. Loading it defines everything and starts
\ nothing; the front end calls run-frames with its own frame word.
\
\ The four maze layouts, their tunnel and wall colors, the maze for each
\ level, the fruit's entrance, pen and exit routes and its bounce, the fruit
\ table, the scatter behaviour of Blinky and Pinky and the tunnel slowdown are
\ transcribed from src/maps.js, src/fruit.js and src/Ghost.js of Shaun
\ LeBron's pacman.js (https://github.com/masonicGIT/pacman, GPL-3.0), whose
\ fruit routes follow Bart Grantham's annotated disassembly of the arcade
\ program. The speeds, the scatter and chase schedule, the ghosts' chase
\ targets, the ghost house counters and Cruise Elroy follow Jamey Pittman's
\ "The Pac-Man Dossier" (100% speed is 75.7576 pixels per second).
\ Positions are maze pixels, x from the left and y from the top; tile t
\ covers pixels 8t to 8t + 7. Directions are 0 up, 1 left, 2 down, 3 right,
\ which is also the arcade's tie-break order.

5 seed

224 288 screen-size 3 screen-zoom :black paper

